{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CFjx5ftcv8FZPinGcWJgPC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<!-- gsd:loop-host\n2\tstep: execute\n3\tpoints: execute:pre, execute:wave:pre, execute:wave:post, execute:post\n4\tagent-roles: executor, verifier, code-reviewer\n5\tproduces: SUMMARY.md\n6\tconsumes: PLAN.md\n7\t-->\n8\t<purpose>\n9\tExecute all plans in a phase using wave-based parallel execution. Orchestrator stays lean — delegates plan execution to subagents.\n10\t</purpose>\n11\t\n12\t<core_principle>\n13\tOrchestrator coordinates, not executes. Each subagent loads the full execute-plan context. Orchestrator: discover plans → analyze deps → group waves → spawn agents → handle checkpoints → collect results.\n14\t</core_principle>\n15\t\n16\t<!-- #2508 runtime-aware-dispatch -->\n17\t\n18\t> **Runtime-aware dispatch (#2508 Phase 4).** GSD workflows dispatch specialized subagents by role. Before dispatching on a built-in-only runtime (kimi-code — three built-ins only), resolve the role to a built-in via `gsd_run query resolve-dispatch-type --requested <role> --raw`. On named-dispatch runtimes (Claude/OpenCode/…) the role is returned unchanged; on kimi-code it maps to `coder`/`explore`/`plan` by role-suffix. The persona rides `${AGENT_SKILLS_<ROLE>}` (Phase 3) regardless. See @gsd-core/references/runtime-aware-dispatch.md.\n19\t\n20\t<runtime_compatibility>\n21\t**Subagent spawning is runtime-specific:**\n22\t- **Claude Code:** Uses `Agent(subagent_type=\"gsd-executor\", ...)` — backgrounded by default; verify completion\n23\t- **Copilot:** Subagent spawning does not reliably return completion signals. **Default to\n24\t  sequential inline execution**: read and follow execute-plan.md directly for each plan\n25\t  instead of spawning parallel agents. Only attempt parallel spawning if the user\n26\t  explicitly requests it — and in that case, rely on the spot-check fallback in step 3\n27\t  to detect completion.\n28\t- **Codex:** native subagent sessions can end abnormally (`turn_aborted`) after the plan\n29\t  work is already committed. Completion is decided by the step-4 artifact reconciliation\n30\t  (SUMMARY + matching recent commits), not by the session's terminal state (#4217).\n31\t- **Other runtimes:** If `Agent`/`agent` tool is genuinely unavailable (e.g. a backgrounded\n32\t  Claude Code agent per #853, or a non-Claude runtime), use sequential inline execution as\n33\t  the fallback for executor parallelization only. If `Agent` IS available (top-level Claude\n34\t  Code), you MUST spawn gsd-executor agents — inline execution is not authorized. Check for\n35\t  actual tool availability, not runtime name.\n36\t\n37\t**Fallback rule:** If a spawned agent completes its work (commits visible, SUMMARY.md exists) but\n38\tthe orchestrator never receives the completion signal, treat it as successful based on spot-checks\n39\tand continue to the next wave/plan. Never block indefinitely waiting for a signal — always verify\n40\tvia filesystem and git state.\n41\t</runtime_compatibility>\n42\t\n43\t<required_reading>\n44\tRead STATE.md before any operation to load project context.\n45\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/agent-contracts.md\n46\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/context-budget.md\n47\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/gates.md\n48\t</required_reading>\n49\t\n50\t<available_agent_types>\n51\tThese are the valid GSD subagent types registered in .claude/agents/ (or equivalent for your runtime).\n52\tAlways use the exact name from this list — do not fall back to 'general-purpose' or other built-in types:\n53\t\n54\t- gsd-executor — Executes plan tasks, commits, creates SUMMARY.md\n55\t- gsd-verifier — Verifies phase completion, checks quality gates\n56\t- gsd-planner — Creates detailed plans from phase scope\n57\t- gsd-phase-researcher — Researches technical approaches for a phase\n58\t- gsd-plan-checker — Reviews plan quality before execution\n59\t- gsd-debugger — Diagnoses and fixes issues\n60\t- gsd-codebase-mapper — Maps project structure and dependencies\n61\t- gsd-integration-checker — Checks cross-phase integration\n62\t- gsd-nyquist-auditor — Validates verification coverage\n63\t- gsd-ui-researcher — Researches UI/UX approaches\n64\t- gsd-ui-checker — Reviews UI implementation quality\n65\t- gsd-ui-auditor — Audits UI against design requirements\n66\t</available_agent_types>\n67\t\n68\t<process>\n69\t\n70\t**Compact Content Gate.** Read and follow `gsd-core/references/compact-content-gate.md` now — it states the `workflow.compact_content` check and the resolution rule this spine defers to. When it directs a Read, read `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/detail/elaboration.md` in full before continuing past this point; its content elaborates on two steps below (check_interactive_mode, cross_ai_delegation).\n71\t\n72\t<step name=\"parse_args\" priority=\"first\">\n73\tParse `$ARGUMENTS` before loading any context:\n74\t\n75\t- First positional token → `PHASE_ARG`\n76\t- Optional `--wave N` → `WAVE_FILTER`\n77\t- Optional `--gaps-only` keeps its current meaning\n78\t- Optional `--cross-ai` → `CROSS_AI_FORCE=true` (force all plans through cross-AI execution)\n79\t- Optional `--no-cross-ai` → `CROSS_AI_DISABLED=true` (disable cross-AI for this run, overrides config and frontmatter)\n80\t\n81\tIf `--wave` is absent, preserve the current behavior of executing all incomplete waves in the phase.\n82\t</step>\n83\t\n84\t<step name=\"initialize\" priority=\"first\">\n85\tLoad all context in one call:\n86\t\n87\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/gsd-run-resolver.md\n88\t\n89\t```bash\n90\tIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END' || true\n91\t$ARGUMENTS\n92\tGSD_ARGS_END\n93\tGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\n94\tWAVE_PARAM=\"\"; if [[ \"$GSD_ARGS\" =~ (^|[[:space:]])--wave[[:space:]]+([^[:space:]-][^[:space:]]*) ]]; then WAVE_PARAM=\"--wave ${BASH_REMATCH[2]}\"; fi\n95\tGSD_WS=$(echo \" $GSD_ARGS\" | sed -nE 's/.* --ws +([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*).*/--ws \\1/p' | head -n 1)\n96\tINIT=$(gsd_run query init.execute-phase ${GSD_WS:+--ws=${GSD_WS##* }} \"${PHASE_ARG}\" $WAVE_PARAM)\n97\tif [[ \"$INIT\" == @file:* ]]; then INIT=$(cat \"${INIT#@file:}\"); fi\n98\tAGENT_SKILLS=$(gsd_run query agent-skills gsd-executor ${GSD_WS:+--ws=${GSD_WS##* }})\n99\t```\n100\t\n101\tParse JSON for: `executor_model`, `verifier_model`, `commit_docs`, `parallelization`, `branching_strategy`, `branch_name`, `phase_found`, `phase_dir`, `phase_number`, `padded_phase`, `phase_name`, `phase_slug`, `plans`, `incomplete_plans`, `plan_count`, `incomplete_count`, `state_exists`, `roadmap_exists`, `phase_req_ids`, `response_language`, `requirements_path`, `section_manifest`, `threat_id_duplicate_count`.\n102\t\n103\t**Threat-ID gate (#4683):** if `threat_id_duplicate_count` is non-zero, read and execute `execute-phase/steps/threat-id-gate.md` BEFORE any dispatch — it is a hard stop (the full duplicate list is in `threat_id_duplicates`).\n104\t\n105\t`section_manifest` (#2932) gates the three `steps/*.md` reads below: read a step file only when its `id` is in `section_manifest.included` (equivalently, its path is in `section_manifest.read`); skip it — without reading — when its `id` is in `section_manifest.excluded`. When `section_manifest` is `null` (degraded: manifest artifact missing/unreadable), read all three unconditionally — the safe superset.\n106\t\n107\t**Model resolution:** If `executor_model` is `\"inherit\"`, omit the `model=` parameter from all `Agent()` calls — do NOT pass `model=\"inherit\"` to Agent. Omitting the `model=` parameter causes Claude Code to inherit the orchestrator model automatically. Only set `model=` when `executor_model` is an explicit model name (e.g., `\"claude-sonnet-5\"`, `\"claude-opus-4-8\"`).\n108\t\n109\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-response-language.md\n110\t\n111\tReset the wave-failure tally (#4915). Fenced `bash` blocks are separate shells, so the post-merge gate's cumulative count reaches step 5.8 through a handoff file; a previous run's tally must not leak in:\n112\t\n113\t```bash\n114\t# gsd-handoff:begin wave-failure-reset\n115\t_GSD_HANDOFF=\"$( { git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir 2>/dev/null || echo \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gsd-$(pwd | cksum | cut -d' ' -f1)\"; } )/gsd-handoff\"; mkdir -p \"$_GSD_HANDOFF\"\n116\t: > \"$_GSD_HANDOFF/wave-failures\"\n117\t# gsd-handoff:end wave-failure-reset\n118\t```\n119\t\n120\tRead runtime/worktree config and fail closed before any executor dispatch:\n121\t\n122\t```bash\n123\tRUNTIME=$(gsd_run query config-get runtime --default claude --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"claude\")\n124\tUSE_WORKTREES=$(gsd_run query config-get workflow.use_worktrees --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"true\")\n125\tEXECUTOR_STALL_INTERVAL_MINUTES=$(gsd_run query config-get executor.stall_detect_interval_minutes --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"5\")\n126\tEXECUTOR_STALL_THRESHOLD_MINUTES=$(gsd_run query config-get executor.stall_threshold_minutes --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"10\")\n127\t\n128\t# Resolve ISOLATION + apply its guards: read and execute the \"Resolve ISOLATION\"\n129\t# section of execute-phase/steps/executor-isolation-dispatch.md. It sets\n130\t# ISOLATION (harness-worktree|orchestrator-worktree|none), forces none when\n131\t# USE_WORKTREES=false, fails closed when a host has no primitive, sweeps orphans,\n132\t# and applies the #683 fork-base auto-degrade.\n133\t```\n134\t\n135\t`ISOLATION` — not `RUNTIME` — is the ONLY fan-out branch point; **never add a `RUNTIME = \"codex\"` test here.** Per-host dispatch detail lives in `execute-phase/steps/executor-isolation-dispatch.md` (read from step 3).\n136\t\n137\tIf the project uses git submodules, worktree isolation is unsafe **only when a plan touches a submodule path** — the executor commit protocol cannot correctly handle submodule commits inside isolated worktrees. Compute submodule paths once and intersect them per-plan with the plan's declared `files_modified` frontmatter.\n138\t\n139\t```bash\n140\t# Parse submodule paths from .gitmodules once (empty if no .gitmodules).\n141\t# SUBMODULE_PATHS is a newline-separated list of repo-relative paths.\n142\tif [ -f .gitmodules ]; then\n143\t  SUBMODULE_PATHS=$(git config --file .gitmodules --get-regexp '^submodule\\..*\\.path$' 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $2}')\n144\telse\n145\t  SUBMODULE_PATHS=\"\"\n146\tfi\n147\t```\n148\t\n149\t`SUBMODULE_PATHS` is exported to the `execute_waves` step, where the per-plan decision happens (see \"Per-plan worktree decision\" sub-step inside `execute_waves`). The decision is per-plan because different plans in the same wave can touch different files — only plans whose paths intersect a submodule must drop worktree isolation; plans nowhere near a submodule keep parallel isolation.\n150\t\n151\tWhen `USE_WORKTREES` is `false`, `ISOLATION` is forced to `none`: executors run sequentially on the main working tree. The per-plan decision below has no effect when worktrees are project-disabled.\n152\t\n153\t`USE_WORKTREES` and `ISOLATION` are also reset for the run when `worktree base-check` detects the orchestrator HEAD has diverged from the worktree fork base (#683) — read and follow `execute-phase/steps/worktree-base-check.md` for the degrade semantics and the `worktree.baseRef:\"head\"` escape hatch (#3659).\n154\t\n155\tRead context window size for adaptive prompt enrichment:\n156\t\n157\t```bash\n158\tCONTEXT_WINDOW=$(gsd_run query config-get context_window --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"200000\")\n159\t```\n160\t\n161\tWhen `CONTEXT_WINDOW >= 500000` (1M-class models), subagent prompts include richer context:\n162\t- Executor agents receive prior wave SUMMARY.md files and the phase CONTEXT.md/RESEARCH.md\n163\t- Verifier agents receive all PLAN.md, SUMMARY.md, CONTEXT.md files plus REQUIREMENTS.md\n164\t- This enables cross-phase awareness and history-aware verification\n165\t\n166\tWhen `CONTEXT_WINDOW < 200000` (sub-200K models), subagent prompts are thinned to reduce static overhead:\n167\t- Executor agents omit extended deviation rule examples and checkpoint examples from inline prompt — load on-demand via @~/.claude/gsd-core/references/executor-examples.md\n168\t- Planner agents omit extended anti-pattern lists and specificity examples from inline prompt — load on-demand via @~/.claude/gsd-core/references/planner-antipatterns.md\n169\t- Core rules and decision logic remain inline; only verbose examples and edge-case lists are extracted\n170\t- This reduces executor static overhead by ~40% while preserving behavioral correctness\n171\t\n172\t**If `phase_found` is false:** Error — phase directory not found.\n173\t**If `plan_count` is 0:** Error — no plans found in phase.\n174\t**If `state_exists` is false but `.planning/` exists:** Offer reconstruct or continue.\n175\t\n176\tWhen `parallelization` is false, plans within a wave execute sequentially.\n177\t\n178\t**Runtime detection for Copilot:**\n179\tCheck if the current runtime is Copilot by testing for the `@gsd-executor` agent pattern\n180\tor absence of the `Agent()` subagent API. If running under Copilot, force sequential inline\n181\texecution regardless of the `parallelization` setting — Copilot's subagent completion\n182\tsignals are unreliable (see `<runtime_compatibility>`). Set `COPILOT_SEQUENTIAL=true`\n183\tinternally and skip the `execute_waves` step in favor of `check_interactive_mode`'s\n184\tinline path for each plan.\n185\t\n186\t**REQUIRED — Sync chain flag with intent.** If user invoked manually (no `--auto`), clear the ephemeral chain flag from any previous interrupted `--auto` chain. This prevents stale `_auto_chain_active: true` from causing unwanted auto-advance. This does NOT touch `workflow.auto_advance` (the user's persistent settings preference). You MUST execute this bash block before any config reads:\n187\t```bash\n188\tIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END' || true\n189\t$ARGUMENTS\n190\tGSD_ARGS_END\n191\tGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\n192\t# REQUIRED: prevents stale auto-chain from previous --auto runs\n193\tif [[ ! \"$GSD_ARGS\" =~ --auto ]]; then\n194\t  gsd_run query config-set workflow._auto_chain_active false || true\n195\tfi\n196\t```\n197\t\n198\tResolve `MVP_MODE` once via the centralized `phase.mvp-mode` query verb (precedence chain: CLI flag → ROADMAP `**Mode:** mvp` → `workflow.mvp_mode` config → false):\n199\t```bash\n200\tIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END' || true\n201\t$ARGUMENTS\n202\tGSD_ARGS_END\n203\tGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\n204\tMVP_FLAG_ARG=\"\"\n205\tif [[ \"$GSD_ARGS\" =~ (^|[[:space:]])--mvp([[:space:]]|$) ]]; then MVP_FLAG_ARG=\"--cli-flag\"; fi\n206\tMVP_MODE=$(gsd_run query phase.mvp-mode \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" $MVP_FLAG_ARG --pick active)\n207\tEXECUTE_POST_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:post --raw)\n208\tTDD_MODE=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:post --active-cap tdd)\n209\t```\n210\t\n211\tA `contribution` hook at this point with `into: code-reviewer` (#4790) is not dispatched from this envelope: `code-review.md` reads it itself and hands it to `gsd-code-reviewer` exactly once.\n212\t\n213\t<step name=\"safe_resume_gate\">\n214\tBefore trusting `STATE.md` or dispatching any executor, derive `CURRENT_PLAN_ID`\n215\tfrom the active incomplete plan in `INIT`, then search recent history:\n216\t```bash\n217\tSUMMARY_PATH=\"{phase_dir}/{plan_padded}-SUMMARY.md\"\n218\t# #5164: the plan's commits come from the evaluation-scope resolver (ADR-5057 §4): anchored\n219\t# on the commit SUBJECT, zero-pad tolerant (#4003) and tolerant of a decimal / N-segment /\n220\t# letter-suffixed phase number (#4619, #4748), reachable from THIS branch only, bounded to\n221\t# the latest reachable tag (milestone marker). One `<sha> <subject>` line per commit, newest first.\n222\tPHASE_NUMBER=\"{phase_number}\"\n223\tPLAN_COMMITS=$(gsd_run check evaluation-scope --plan \"${PHASE_NUMBER}-{plan_padded}\" --commits-only --milestone-bound --max-commits 30 --raw 2>/dev/null) && PLAN_SCOPE_RC=0 || PLAN_SCOPE_RC=$?\n224\t# Exit 69 (UNAVAILABLE) = \"could not look\": empty is then NOT \"no commits\". Fail closed (#5170).\n225\tif [ \"$PLAN_SCOPE_RC\" -ne 0 ]; then echo \"SAFE-RESUME GATE: could not resolve the plan's commits (evaluation-scope exit ${PLAN_SCOPE_RC}); not dispatching an executor on an unknown resume state.\" >&2; exit 1; fi\n226\tPLAN_COMMITS=$(printf '%s' \"$PLAN_COMMITS\" | node -e \"let s='';process.stdin.on('data',d=>s+=d).on('end',()=>{try{process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(s).commits.map(c=>c.sha.slice(0,10)+' '+c.subject).join('\\n'))}catch{}})\")\n227\t```\n228\tIf production commits exist and `SUMMARY.md is missing` (no `.planning/async-jobs/*.json` manifest matches it: a match is a legal `external_job_waiting` deferral - reconcile per `docs/reference/planning-artifacts.md`, never re-dispatch), stop before spawning a\n229\tnew executor; continuing risks duplicate work and stale `STATE.md`/ROADMAP progress.\n230\tOffer these recovery options:\n231\t- `close out manually` — inspect commits, write SUMMARY.md, then update STATE/ROADMAP.\n232\t- `re-execute from scratch` — revert or supersede partial commits before dispatch.\n233\t- `mark-and-skip` — record the anomaly and move on only with explicit confirmation.\n234\t</step>\n235\t\n236\t**TDD gate.** Task-scoped enforcement runs inside plan execution (immediately before each implementation step), where `TASK_FILE`, `PLAN_ID`, and `TASK_ID` are defined. #4011: the gate keys on `TDD_MODE` ALONE — a discipline gate coupled to the product-scope `MVP_MODE` flag was silently inert on every non-MVP phase, contradicting `gsd-core/references/tdd.md`'s contract that `workflow.tdd_mode` binds for all `type: tdd` plans. MVP mode remains free to imply TDD; it is no longer required by it. Keep the same predicate and RED-commit contract:\n237\t```bash\n238\tif [ \"$TDD_MODE\" = \"true\" ]; then\n239\t  IS_BEHAVIOR_ADDING=$(gsd_run query task.is-behavior-adding \"$TASK_FILE\" --pick is_behavior_adding)\n240\t  if [ \"$IS_BEHAVIOR_ADDING\" = \"true\" ]; then\n241\t    # #5164: the same resolver, scope and milestone bound as safe_resume_gate — anchored,\n242\t    # zero-pad tolerant (#4003, #4619, #4748), this branch only. A padded literal grep\n243\t    # hard-halted on a correct unpadded RED commit.\n244\t    # #4379: this pathspec IS the gate's definition of \"a test file\". It was\n245\t    # JS/TS-only, so Go tripped on every task; and `**/` never matches a\n246\t    # root-level path, so a root `foo.test.js` was invisible too. Bare globs\n247\t    # match at every depth. NOT widened to ordinary source — that would make\n248\t    # the gate pass on any in-scope commit. Trade-offs and the Rust gap:\n249\t    # references/tdd.md § Create first test file.\n250\t\n251\t    RED_COMMIT=$(gsd_run check evaluation-scope --plan \"${PHASE_NUMBER}-${PLAN_ID}\" --commits-only --milestone-bound --max-commits 1 --raw --pathspec \"*.test.*\" --pathspec \"*.spec.*\" --pathspec \"tests/\" --pathspec \"__tests__/\" --pathspec \"*_test.go\" --pathspec \"test_*.py\" --pathspec \"*_test.py\" --pathspec \"*_test.exs\" --pathspec \"*_spec.rb\" --pathspec \"*_test.rb\" 2>/dev/null) && RED_SCOPE_RC=0 || RED_SCOPE_RC=$?\n252\t    # Exit 69 (UNAVAILABLE) = the scope could not be resolved: that is not \"missing RED commit\" (#5170).\n253\t    if [ \"$RED_SCOPE_RC\" -ne 0 ]; then echo \"TDD GATE UNAVAILABLE: could not resolve the plan's commits for ${PLAN_ID}/${TASK_ID} (evaluation-scope exit ${RED_SCOPE_RC})\"; exit 1; fi\n254\t    RED_COMMIT=$(printf '%s' \"$RED_COMMIT\" | node -e \"let s='';process.stdin.on('data',d=>s+=d).on('end',()=>{try{const c=JSON.parse(s).commits;process.stdout.write(c.length?c[0].sha.slice(0,10)+' '+c[0].subject:'')}catch{}})\")\n255\t    if [ -z \"$RED_COMMIT\" ]; then\n256\t      gsd_run query state.update last_gate_trip \"${PLAN_ID}/${TASK_ID}\" || true\n257\t      echo \"TDD GATE TRIPPED: missing RED commit for ${PLAN_ID}/${TASK_ID}\"\n258\t      exit 1\n259\t    fi\n260\t  fi\n261\tfi\n262\t```\n263\tPure doc-only / config-only / test-only tasks return `is_behavior_adding=false` and are exempt. When the gate trips, Read `$HOME/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-mvp-tdd.md` for the exact halt report format.\n264\t</step>\n265\t\n266\t<step name=\"check_blocking_antipatterns\" priority=\"first\">\n267\t**MANDATORY — Check for blocking anti-patterns before any other work.**\n268\t\n269\tLook for a `.continue-here.md` in the current phase directory:\n270\t\n271\t```bash\n272\tls ${phase_dir}/.continue-here.md 2>/dev/null || true\n273\t```\n274\t\n275\tIf `.continue-here.md` exists, parse its \"Critical Anti-Patterns\" table for rows with `severity` = `blocking`.\n276\t\n277\t**If one or more `blocking` anti-patterns are found:**\n278\t\n279\tThis step cannot be skipped. Before proceeding to `check_interactive_mode` or any other step, the agent must demonstrate understanding of each blocking anti-pattern by answering all three questions for each one:\n280\t\n281\t1. **What is this anti-pattern?** — Describe it in your own words, not by quoting the handoff.\n282\t2. **How did it manifest?** — Explain the specific failure that caused it to be recorded.\n283\t3. **What structural mechanism (not acknowledgment) prevents it?** — Name the concrete step, checklist item, or enforcement mechanism that stops recurrence.\n284\t\n285\tWrite these answers inline before continuing. If a blocking anti-pattern cannot be answered from the context in `.continue-here.md`, stop and ask the user for clarification.\n286\t\n287\t**If no `.continue-here.md` exists, or no `blocking` rows are found:** Proceed directly to `check_interactive_mode`.\n288\t</step>\n289\t\n290\t<step name=\"check_interactive_mode\">\n291\t**Parse `--interactive` flag from $ARGUMENTS.** If present, switch to interactive execution mode: plans run sequentially **inline** (no subagent spawning, ignoring wave grouping), reading `execute-plan.md` directly rather than dispatching `gsd-executor`. **Once per plan** (not per task), present a 4-option menu (execute / review-first / skip / stop) before starting that plan's tasks. Once executing, tasks run one at a time with only a brief pause after each — the agent stops mid-plan only if the user actually types something, it does not re-show the menu. After all plans, proceed to verification as normal. Full flow (the exact presentation format, the review-first sub-branch): `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/detail/elaboration.md` § 1.\n292\t\n293\t**Skip to handle_branching step** (interactive plans execute inline after grouping).\n294\t</step>\n295\t\n296\t<step name=\"handle_branching\">\n297\tCheck `branching_strategy` from init:\n298\t\n299\t**\"none\":** Read and execute `execute-phase/steps/protected-branch.md`.\n300\t\n301\t**\"phase\" or \"milestone\":** Use pre-computed `branch_name` from init.\n302\t\n303\tFork the new phase branch off `origin/HEAD` (the project's default branch), not the current HEAD — otherwise consecutive phases compound and stay unpushed (#2916). If `$BRANCH_NAME` already exists locally, reuse it as-is.\n304\t\n305\t```bash\n306\tDEFAULT_BRANCH=$(gsd_run query git.base-branch 2>/dev/null \\\n307\t  || git symbolic-ref --quiet --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null | sed 's|^origin/||' \\\n308\t  || echo main)\n309\t\n310\tif git show-ref --verify --quiet \"refs/heads/$BRANCH_NAME\"; then\n311\t  git switch \"$BRANCH_NAME\" || { echo \"ERROR: Could not switch to existing branch '$BRANCH_NAME'.\" >&2; exit 1; }\n312\telse\n313\t  if ! git fetch --quiet origin \"$DEFAULT_BRANCH\"; then  # #2916\n314\t    git show-ref --verify --quiet \"refs/remotes/origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" \\\n315\t      || { echo \"ERROR: fetch origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH failed and no local copy exists. Refusing to create '$BRANCH_NAME' off current HEAD (#2916).\" >&2; exit 1; }\n316\t    echo \"WARNING: fetch origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH failed; using local copy as base.\" >&2\n317\t  fi\n318\t  if [ -n \"$(git status --porcelain)\" ]; then\n319\t    echo \"WARNING: Uncommitted changes will be carried onto '$BRANCH_NAME' (branched off origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH, not previous HEAD).\"\n320\t  else\n321\t    git switch --quiet \"$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null && git merge --ff-only --quiet \"origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || true\n322\t  fi\n323\t  # Pinned base (#2916); --no-track (#2498). #2639: warn if local ahead of origin.\n324\t  AHEAD=$(git rev-list --count \"origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH..$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n325\t  [ \"$AHEAD\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$AHEAD\" ] && echo \"WARNING: $DEFAULT_BRANCH is $AHEAD ahead of origin — '$BRANCH_NAME' won't include those commits (#2639).\" >&2\n326\t  git checkout -b \"$BRANCH_NAME\" \"origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" --no-track \\\n327\t    || { echo \"ERROR: Could not create '$BRANCH_NAME' from origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH (#2916).\" >&2; exit 1; }\n328\tfi\n329\t```\n330\t\n331\tAll subsequent commits go to this branch. User handles merging.\n332\t</step>\n333\t\n334\t<step name=\"validate_phase\">\n335\tFrom init JSON: `phase_dir`, `plan_count`, `incomplete_count`.\n336\t\n337\tReport: \"Found {plan_count} plans in {phase_dir} ({incomplete_count} incomplete)\"\n338\t\n339\t**Update STATE.md for phase start:**\n340\t```bash\n341\tgsd_run query state.begin-phase --phase \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" --name \"${PHASE_NAME}\" --plans \"${PLAN_COUNT}\"\n342\t```\n343\tThis updates Status, Last Activity, Current focus, Current Position, and plan counts in STATE.md so frontmatter and body text reflect the active phase immediately.\n344\t</step>\n345\t\n346\t<step name=\"discover_and_group_plans\">\n347\tLoad plan inventory with wave grouping in one call:\n348\t\n349\t```bash\n350\tPLAN_INDEX=$(gsd_run query phase-plan-index \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")\n351\t```\n352\t\n353\tParse JSON for: `phase`, `plans[]`, `waves`, `incomplete`, `runnable`, `ready_plans`, `has_checkpoints` — full per-plan fields and the #4628 readiness rules: read and follow `execute-phase/steps/ready-wave-gate.md`.\n354\t\n355\t**Filtering:** Skip plans where `has_summary: true`. Additionally skip any plan whose `blocked_by` array is non-empty (#2830) — it depends, directly or transitively, on a plan that halted at a designed stop rather than completing — and report it by name: \"Skipping {plan.id}: blocked by halted {blocked_by.join(', ')}\". Never silently drop a blocked plan from the report; it must appear by name with its reason, not merely vanish from the executable list. This rule is additive to the `has_summary` skip, not a replacement for it. Additionally skip any incomplete plan with `ready: false` (#4628 — see `execute-phase/steps/ready-wave-gate.md`; never dispatch a not-ready plan). If `--gaps-only`: also skip plans whose `gap_closure` is not `true` — but first confirm every plan object carries a `gap_closure` key. If any lacks it, the index cannot answer the filter (an older gsd-tools): STOP and report \"--gaps-only cannot read gap_closure from phase-plan-index — refusing to report an empty selection\" rather than filtering. A key the index never emitted must not surface as \"No matching incomplete plans\" (#4924). If `WAVE_FILTER` is set: also skip plans whose `wave` does not equal `WAVE_FILTER`.\n356\t\n357\t**Wave safety check:** If `WAVE_FILTER` is set and there are still incomplete plans in any lower wave that match the current execution mode, STOP and tell the user to finish earlier waves first. Do not let Wave 2+ execute while prerequisite earlier-wave plans remain incomplete.\n358\t\n359\t**If all filtered — do NOT exit unconditionally (#2868).** \"No plan work left\" and \"phase fully\n360\tdone\" are different conditions: a run can be interrupted between the final wave's SUMMARY and\n361\t`verify_phase_goal` (most commonly by a checkpoint plan that is retired but still writes a SUMMARY),\n362\tleaving a phase that looks complete from every index yet never produced `*-VERIFICATION.md`. A\n363\tthird condition looks identical to the first two by plan_count alone but is neither: some filtered\n364\tplans were filtered because they are **blocked** (non-empty `blocked_by`, #2830), not because they\n365\tare done. Blocked-and-incomplete must never be reported as finished.\n366\t\n367\t```bash\n368\t# #5118: the owner's answer — `status` and the bare command it routes to. A non-zero exit\n369\t# (an out-of-set report status) is a hard error: surface it, never read it as \"no status\".\n370\tVERIFY_STATUS=$(gsd_run query verification status \"${PHASE_DIR}\" --pick status) || { echo \"verification status failed — see the error above\" >&2; exit 1; }\n371\tVERIFY_ROUTE=$(gsd_run query verification status \"${PHASE_DIR}\" --pick route) || { echo \"verification status failed — see the error above\" >&2; exit 1; }\n372\t# #3684: checkbox = marked-complete; report fields can claim a no-op write (#3685).\n373\tANALYZE=$(gsd_run query roadmap.analyze)\n374\tif [[ \"$ANALYZE\" == @file:* ]]; then ANALYZE=$(cat \"${ANALYZE#@file:}\"); fi\n375\tPHASE_MARKED=$(echo \"$ANALYZE\"|jq -r --arg p \"$PHASE_NUMBER\" 'def n:sub(\"^0+(?=[0-9])\";\"\");.phases[]|select(((.number//.phase_number|tostring|n))==($p|n))|.roadmap_complete'|head -1)\n376\t```\n377\t\n378\tEvaluate in this exact order — the first matching condition decides the outcome; do not evaluate\n379\tlater conditions once one matches:\n380\t\n381\t1. **A filter is active** (`--gaps-only`, or `WAVE_FILTER` set): report \"No matching incomplete\n382\t   plans\" → exit, unchanged. A filtered run finding nothing left in ITS slice says nothing about\n383\t   whether the phase as a whole is done, and must never jump to verification.\n384\t2. **No filter is active, and at least one filtered plan was skipped because of a non-empty\n385\t   `blocked_by`** (irrespective of `VERIFY_STATUS`): the phase is NOT finished — it is **stuck on a\n386\t   halt**. A plan with no SUMMARY and no dispatched work must never be treated as done merely\n387\t   because nothing was left to filter. Report:\n388\t   `\"Phase stuck: {blocked plan ids} blocked by halted {their blocked_by ids} — resolve the halt, do not resume verification.\"`\n389\t   → exit. Do not fall through to condition 3; this is not a completion state.\n390\t2b. **No filter is active, no blocked-plan skip occurred, and at least one filtered plan was skipped because `ready: false` (#4628)** — the phase is WAITING on incomplete predecessors, not finished: report it by name and exit before any completion state (`execute-phase/steps/ready-wave-gate.md`).\n391\t3. **No filter is active, and every filtered plan was filtered by `has_summary` alone** (no\n392\t   blocked-plan skip occurred) — branch on the owner's answer, never on a status word (#5118):\n393\t   - **`VERIFY_ROUTE == execute-phase`** — the owner routes here when the verify step never ran\n394\t     (`VERIFY_STATUS == missing`, #2868) and when covered source changed after the verifier ran\n395\t     (#4682); on both sides of `PHASE_MARKED`. Report `$VERIFY_STATUS` with:\n396\t     `\"All {plan_count} plans are summarized but no VERIFICATION.md exists — resuming at the phase gates (#2868).\"`\n397\t     (or, for a stale report, \"…verification is stale — resuming at the phase gates to re-run the verifier (#4682).\")\n398\t     SKIP `cross_ai_delegation`, `execute_waves` and `checkpoint_handling` — there is no wave work\n399\t     to do — and continue directly at `aggregate_results`, NOT `code_review_gate`. `aggregate_results`\n400\t     reads exclusively from on-disk `${PHASE_DIR}` artifacts (`*-SUMMARY.md`) and independent"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"uuid-4","uuid":"uuid-86","timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:00:37.032Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"~/.claude/gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase.md","content":"<!-- gsd:loop-host\nstep: execute\npoints: execute:pre, execute:wave:pre, execute:wave:post, execute:post\nagent-roles: executor, verifier, code-reviewer\nproduces: SUMMARY.md\nconsumes: PLAN.md\n-->\n<purpose>\nExecute all plans in a phase using wave-based parallel execution. Orchestrator stays lean — delegates plan execution to subagents.\n</purpose>\n\n<core_principle>\nOrchestrator coordinates, not executes. Each subagent loads the full execute-plan context. Orchestrator: discover plans → analyze deps → group waves → spawn agents → handle checkpoints → collect results.\n</core_principle>\n\n<!-- #2508 runtime-aware-dispatch -->\n\n> **Runtime-aware dispatch (#2508 Phase 4).** GSD workflows dispatch specialized subagents by role. Before dispatching on a built-in-only runtime (kimi-code — three built-ins only), resolve the role to a built-in via `gsd_run query resolve-dispatch-type --requested <role> --raw`. On named-dispatch runtimes (Claude/OpenCode/…) the role is returned unchanged; on kimi-code it maps to `coder`/`explore`/`plan` by role-suffix. The persona rides `${AGENT_SKILLS_<ROLE>}` (Phase 3) regardless. See @gsd-core/references/runtime-aware-dispatch.md.\n\n<runtime_compatibility>\n**Subagent spawning is runtime-specific:**\n- **Claude Code:** Uses `Agent(subagent_type=\"gsd-executor\", ...)` — backgrounded by default; verify completion\n- **Copilot:** Subagent spawning does not reliably return completion signals. **Default to\n  sequential inline execution**: read and follow execute-plan.md directly for each plan\n  instead of spawning parallel agents. Only attempt parallel spawning if the user\n  explicitly requests it — and in that case, rely on the spot-check fallback in step 3\n  to detect completion.\n- **Codex:** native subagent sessions can end abnormally (`turn_aborted`) after the plan\n  work is already committed. Completion is decided by the step-4 artifact reconciliation\n  (SUMMARY + matching recent commits), not by the session's terminal state (#4217).\n- **Other runtimes:** If `Agent`/`agent` tool is genuinely unavailable (e.g. a backgrounded\n  Claude Code agent per #853, or a non-Claude runtime), use sequential inline execution as\n  the fallback for executor parallelization only. If `Agent` IS available (top-level Claude\n  Code), you MUST spawn gsd-executor agents — inline execution is not authorized. Check for\n  actual tool availability, not runtime name.\n\n**Fallback rule:** If a spawned agent completes its work (commits visible, SUMMARY.md exists) but\nthe orchestrator never receives the completion signal, treat it as successful based on spot-checks\nand continue to the next wave/plan. Never block indefinitely waiting for a signal — always verify\nvia filesystem and git state.\n</runtime_compatibility>\n\n<required_reading>\nRead STATE.md before any operation to load project context.\n@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/agent-contracts.md\n@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/context-budget.md\n@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/gates.md\n</required_reading>\n\n<available_agent_types>\nThese are the valid GSD subagent types registered in .claude/agents/ (or equivalent for your runtime).\nAlways use the exact name from this list — do not fall back to 'general-purpose' or other built-in types:\n\n- gsd-executor — Executes plan tasks, commits, creates SUMMARY.md\n- gsd-verifier — Verifies phase completion, checks quality gates\n- gsd-planner — Creates detailed plans from phase scope\n- gsd-phase-researcher — Researches technical approaches for a phase\n- gsd-plan-checker — Reviews plan quality before execution\n- gsd-debugger — Diagnoses and fixes issues\n- gsd-codebase-mapper — Maps project structure and dependencies\n- gsd-integration-checker — Checks cross-phase integration\n- gsd-nyquist-auditor — Validates verification coverage\n- gsd-ui-researcher — Researches UI/UX approaches\n- gsd-ui-checker — Reviews UI implementation quality\n- gsd-ui-auditor — Audits UI against design requirements\n</available_agent_types>\n\n<process>\n\n**Compact Content Gate.** Read and follow `gsd-core/references/compact-content-gate.md` now — it states the `workflow.compact_content` check and the resolution rule this spine defers to. When it directs a Read, read `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/detail/elaboration.md` in full before continuing past this point; its content elaborates on two steps below (check_interactive_mode, cross_ai_delegation).\n\n<step name=\"parse_args\" priority=\"first\">\nParse `$ARGUMENTS` before loading any context:\n\n- First positional token → `PHASE_ARG`\n- Optional `--wave N` → `WAVE_FILTER`\n- Optional `--gaps-only` keeps its current meaning\n- Optional `--cross-ai` → `CROSS_AI_FORCE=true` (force all plans through cross-AI execution)\n- Optional `--no-cross-ai` → `CROSS_AI_DISABLED=true` (disable cross-AI for this run, overrides config and frontmatter)\n\nIf `--wave` is absent, preserve the current behavior of executing all incomplete waves in the phase.\n</step>\n\n<step name=\"initialize\" priority=\"first\">\nLoad all context in one call:\n\n@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/gsd-run-resolver.md\n\n```bash\nIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END' || true\n$ARGUMENTS\nGSD_ARGS_END\nGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\nWAVE_PARAM=\"\"; if [[ \"$GSD_ARGS\" =~ (^|[[:space:]])--wave[[:space:]]+([^[:space:]-][^[:space:]]*) ]]; then WAVE_PARAM=\"--wave ${BASH_REMATCH[2]}\"; fi\nGSD_WS=$(echo \" $GSD_ARGS\" | sed -nE 's/.* --ws +([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*).*/--ws \\1/p' | head -n 1)\nINIT=$(gsd_run query init.execute-phase ${GSD_WS:+--ws=${GSD_WS##* }} \"${PHASE_ARG}\" $WAVE_PARAM)\nif [[ \"$INIT\" == @file:* ]]; then INIT=$(cat \"${INIT#@file:}\"); fi\nAGENT_SKILLS=$(gsd_run query agent-skills gsd-executor ${GSD_WS:+--ws=${GSD_WS##* }})\n```\n\nParse JSON for: `executor_model`, `verifier_model`, `commit_docs`, `parallelization`, `branching_strategy`, `branch_name`, `phase_found`, `phase_dir`, `phase_number`, `padded_phase`, `phase_name`, `phase_slug`, `plans`, `incomplete_plans`, `plan_count`, `incomplete_count`, `state_exists`, `roadmap_exists`, `phase_req_ids`, `response_language`, `requirements_path`, `section_manifest`, `threat_id_duplicate_count`.\n\n**Threat-ID gate (#4683):** if `threat_id_duplicate_count` is non-zero, read and execute `execute-phase/steps/threat-id-gate.md` BEFORE any dispatch — it is a hard stop (the full duplicate list is in `threat_id_duplicates`).\n\n`section_manifest` (#2932) gates the three `steps/*.md` reads below: read a step file only when its `id` is in `section_manifest.included` (equivalently, its path is in `section_manifest.read`); skip it — without reading — when its `id` is in `section_manifest.excluded`. When `section_manifest` is `null` (degraded: manifest artifact missing/unreadable), read all three unconditionally — the safe superset.\n\n**Model resolution:** If `executor_model` is `\"inherit\"`, omit the `model=` parameter from all `Agent()` calls — do NOT pass `model=\"inherit\"` to Agent. Omitting the `model=` parameter causes Claude Code to inherit the orchestrator model automatically. Only set `model=` when `executor_model` is an explicit model name (e.g., `\"claude-sonnet-5\"`, `\"claude-opus-4-8\"`).\n\n@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-response-language.md\n\nReset the wave-failure tally (#4915). Fenced `bash` blocks are separate shells, so the post-merge gate's cumulative count reaches step 5.8 through a handoff file; a previous run's tally must not leak in:\n\n```bash\n# gsd-handoff:begin wave-failure-reset\n_GSD_HANDOFF=\"$( { git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir 2>/dev/null || echo \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gsd-$(pwd | cksum | cut -d' ' -f1)\"; } )/gsd-handoff\"; mkdir -p \"$_GSD_HANDOFF\"\n: > \"$_GSD_HANDOFF/wave-failures\"\n# gsd-handoff:end wave-failure-reset\n```\n\nRead runtime/worktree config and fail closed before any executor dispatch:\n\n```bash\nRUNTIME=$(gsd_run query config-get runtime --default claude --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"claude\")\nUSE_WORKTREES=$(gsd_run query config-get workflow.use_worktrees --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"true\")\nEXECUTOR_STALL_INTERVAL_MINUTES=$(gsd_run query config-get executor.stall_detect_interval_minutes --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"5\")\nEXECUTOR_STALL_THRESHOLD_MINUTES=$(gsd_run query config-get executor.stall_threshold_minutes --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"10\")\n\n# Resolve ISOLATION + apply its guards: read and execute the \"Resolve ISOLATION\"\n# section of execute-phase/steps/executor-isolation-dispatch.md. It sets\n# ISOLATION (harness-worktree|orchestrator-worktree|none), forces none when\n# USE_WORKTREES=false, fails closed when a host has no primitive, sweeps orphans,\n# and applies the #683 fork-base auto-degrade.\n```\n\n`ISOLATION` — not `RUNTIME` — is the ONLY fan-out branch point; **never add a `RUNTIME = \"codex\"` test here.** Per-host dispatch detail lives in `execute-phase/steps/executor-isolation-dispatch.md` (read from step 3).\n\nIf the project uses git submodules, worktree isolation is unsafe **only when a plan touches a submodule path** — the executor commit protocol cannot correctly handle submodule commits inside isolated worktrees. Compute submodule paths once and intersect them per-plan with the plan's declared `files_modified` frontmatter.\n\n```bash\n# Parse submodule paths from .gitmodules once (empty if no .gitmodules).\n# SUBMODULE_PATHS is a newline-separated list of repo-relative paths.\nif [ -f .gitmodules ]; then\n  SUBMODULE_PATHS=$(git config --file .gitmodules --get-regexp '^submodule\\..*\\.path$' 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $2}')\nelse\n  SUBMODULE_PATHS=\"\"\nfi\n```\n\n`SUBMODULE_PATHS` is exported to the `execute_waves` step, where the per-plan decision happens (see \"Per-plan worktree decision\" sub-step inside `execute_waves`). The decision is per-plan because different plans in the same wave can touch different files — only plans whose paths intersect a submodule must drop worktree isolation; plans nowhere near a submodule keep parallel isolation.\n\nWhen `USE_WORKTREES` is `false`, `ISOLATION` is forced to `none`: executors run sequentially on the main working tree. The per-plan decision below has no effect when worktrees are project-disabled.\n\n`USE_WORKTREES` and `ISOLATION` are also reset for the run when `worktree base-check` detects the orchestrator HEAD has diverged from the worktree fork base (#683) — read and follow `execute-phase/steps/worktree-base-check.md` for the degrade semantics and the `worktree.baseRef:\"head\"` escape hatch (#3659).\n\nRead context window size for adaptive prompt enrichment:\n\n```bash\nCONTEXT_WINDOW=$(gsd_run query config-get context_window --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"200000\")\n```\n\nWhen `CONTEXT_WINDOW >= 500000` (1M-class models), subagent prompts include richer context:\n- Executor agents receive prior wave SUMMARY.md files and the phase CONTEXT.md/RESEARCH.md\n- Verifier agents receive all PLAN.md, SUMMARY.md, CONTEXT.md files plus REQUIREMENTS.md\n- This enables cross-phase awareness and history-aware verification\n\nWhen `CONTEXT_WINDOW < 200000` (sub-200K models), subagent prompts are thinned to reduce static overhead:\n- Executor agents omit extended deviation rule examples and checkpoint examples from inline prompt — load on-demand via @~/.claude/gsd-core/references/executor-examples.md\n- Planner agents omit extended anti-pattern lists and specificity examples from inline prompt — load on-demand via @~/.claude/gsd-core/references/planner-antipatterns.md\n- Core rules and decision logic remain inline; only verbose examples and edge-case lists are extracted\n- This reduces executor static overhead by ~40% while preserving behavioral correctness\n\n**If `phase_found` is false:** Error — phase directory not found.\n**If `plan_count` is 0:** Error — no plans found in phase.\n**If `state_exists` is false but `.planning/` exists:** Offer reconstruct or continue.\n\nWhen `parallelization` is false, plans within a wave execute sequentially.\n\n**Runtime detection for Copilot:**\nCheck if the current runtime is Copilot by testing for the `@gsd-executor` agent pattern\nor absence of the `Agent()` subagent API. If running under Copilot, force sequential inline\nexecution regardless of the `parallelization` setting — Copilot's subagent completion\nsignals are unreliable (see `<runtime_compatibility>`). Set `COPILOT_SEQUENTIAL=true`\ninternally and skip the `execute_waves` step in favor of `check_interactive_mode`'s\ninline path for each plan.\n\n**REQUIRED — Sync chain flag with intent.** If user invoked manually (no `--auto`), clear the ephemeral chain flag from any previous interrupted `--auto` chain. This prevents stale `_auto_chain_active: true` from causing unwanted auto-advance. This does NOT touch `workflow.auto_advance` (the user's persistent settings preference). You MUST execute this bash block before any config reads:\n```bash\nIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END' || true\n$ARGUMENTS\nGSD_ARGS_END\nGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\n# REQUIRED: prevents stale auto-chain from previous --auto runs\nif [[ ! \"$GSD_ARGS\" =~ --auto ]]; then\n  gsd_run query config-set workflow._auto_chain_active false || true\nfi\n```\n\nResolve `MVP_MODE` once via the centralized `phase.mvp-mode` query verb (precedence chain: CLI flag → ROADMAP `**Mode:** mvp` → `workflow.mvp_mode` config → false):\n```bash\nIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END' || true\n$ARGUMENTS\nGSD_ARGS_END\nGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\nMVP_FLAG_ARG=\"\"\nif [[ \"$GSD_ARGS\" =~ (^|[[:space:]])--mvp([[:space:]]|$) ]]; then MVP_FLAG_ARG=\"--cli-flag\"; fi\nMVP_MODE=$(gsd_run query phase.mvp-mode \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" $MVP_FLAG_ARG --pick active)\nEXECUTE_POST_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:post --raw)\nTDD_MODE=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:post --active-cap tdd)\n```\n\nA `contribution` hook at this point with `into: code-reviewer` (#4790) is not dispatched from this envelope: `code-review.md` reads it itself and hands it to `gsd-code-reviewer` exactly once.\n\n<step name=\"safe_resume_gate\">\nBefore trusting `STATE.md` or dispatching any executor, derive `CURRENT_PLAN_ID`\nfrom the active incomplete plan in `INIT`, then search recent history:\n```bash\nSUMMARY_PATH=\"{phase_dir}/{plan_padded}-SUMMARY.md\"\n# #5164: the plan's commits come from the evaluation-scope resolver (ADR-5057 §4): anchored\n# on the commit SUBJECT, zero-pad tolerant (#4003) and tolerant of a decimal / N-segment /\n# letter-suffixed phase number (#4619, #4748), reachable from THIS branch only, bounded to\n# the latest reachable tag (milestone marker). One `<sha> <subject>` line per commit, newest first.\nPHASE_NUMBER=\"{phase_number}\"\nPLAN_COMMITS=$(gsd_run check evaluation-scope --plan \"${PHASE_NUMBER}-{plan_padded}\" --commits-only --milestone-bound --max-commits 30 --raw 2>/dev/null) && PLAN_SCOPE_RC=0 || PLAN_SCOPE_RC=$?\n# Exit 69 (UNAVAILABLE) = \"could not look\": empty is then NOT \"no commits\". Fail closed (#5170).\nif [ \"$PLAN_SCOPE_RC\" -ne 0 ]; then echo \"SAFE-RESUME GATE: could not resolve the plan's commits (evaluation-scope exit ${PLAN_SCOPE_RC}); not dispatching an executor on an unknown resume state.\" >&2; exit 1; fi\nPLAN_COMMITS=$(printf '%s' \"$PLAN_COMMITS\" | node -e \"let s='';process.stdin.on('data',d=>s+=d).on('end',()=>{try{process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(s).commits.map(c=>c.sha.slice(0,10)+' '+c.subject).join('\\n'))}catch{}})\")\n```\nIf production commits exist and `SUMMARY.md is missing` (no `.planning/async-jobs/*.json` manifest matches it: a match is a legal `external_job_waiting` deferral - reconcile per `docs/reference/planning-artifacts.md`, never re-dispatch), stop before spawning a\nnew executor; continuing risks duplicate work and stale `STATE.md`/ROADMAP progress.\nOffer these recovery options:\n- `close out manually` — inspect commits, write SUMMARY.md, then update STATE/ROADMAP.\n- `re-execute from scratch` — revert or supersede partial commits before dispatch.\n- `mark-and-skip` — record the anomaly and move on only with explicit confirmation.\n</step>\n\n**TDD gate.** Task-scoped enforcement runs inside plan execution (immediately before each implementation step), where `TASK_FILE`, `PLAN_ID`, and `TASK_ID` are defined. #4011: the gate keys on `TDD_MODE` ALONE — a discipline gate coupled to the product-scope `MVP_MODE` flag was silently inert on every non-MVP phase, contradicting `gsd-core/references/tdd.md`'s contract that `workflow.tdd_mode` binds for all `type: tdd` plans. MVP mode remains free to imply TDD; it is no longer required by it. Keep the same predicate and RED-commit contract:\n```bash\nif [ \"$TDD_MODE\" = \"true\" ]; then\n  IS_BEHAVIOR_ADDING=$(gsd_run query task.is-behavior-adding \"$TASK_FILE\" --pick is_behavior_adding)\n  if [ \"$IS_BEHAVIOR_ADDING\" = \"true\" ]; then\n    # #5164: the same resolver, scope and milestone bound as safe_resume_gate — anchored,\n    # zero-pad tolerant (#4003, #4619, #4748), this branch only. A padded literal grep\n    # hard-halted on a correct unpadded RED commit.\n    # #4379: this pathspec IS the gate's definition of \"a test file\". It was\n    # JS/TS-only, so Go tripped on every task; and `**/` never matches a\n    # root-level path, so a root `foo.test.js` was invisible too. Bare globs\n    # match at every depth. NOT widened to ordinary source — that would make\n    # the gate pass on any in-scope commit. Trade-offs and the Rust gap:\n    # references/tdd.md § Create first test file.\n\n    RED_COMMIT=$(gsd_run check evaluation-scope --plan \"${PHASE_NUMBER}-${PLAN_ID}\" --commits-only --milestone-bound --max-commits 1 --raw --pathspec \"*.test.*\" --pathspec \"*.spec.*\" --pathspec \"tests/\" --pathspec \"__tests__/\" --pathspec \"*_test.go\" --pathspec \"test_*.py\" --pathspec \"*_test.py\" --pathspec \"*_test.exs\" --pathspec \"*_spec.rb\" --pathspec \"*_test.rb\" 2>/dev/null) && RED_SCOPE_RC=0 || RED_SCOPE_RC=$?\n    # Exit 69 (UNAVAILABLE) = the scope could not be resolved: that is not \"missing RED commit\" (#5170).\n    if [ \"$RED_SCOPE_RC\" -ne 0 ]; then echo \"TDD GATE UNAVAILABLE: could not resolve the plan's commits for ${PLAN_ID}/${TASK_ID} (evaluation-scope exit ${RED_SCOPE_RC})\"; exit 1; fi\n    RED_COMMIT=$(printf '%s' \"$RED_COMMIT\" | node -e \"let s='';process.stdin.on('data',d=>s+=d).on('end',()=>{try{const c=JSON.parse(s).commits;process.stdout.write(c.length?c[0].sha.slice(0,10)+' '+c[0].subject:'')}catch{}})\")\n    if [ -z \"$RED_COMMIT\" ]; then\n      gsd_run query state.update last_gate_trip \"${PLAN_ID}/${TASK_ID}\" || true\n      echo \"TDD GATE TRIPPED: missing RED commit for ${PLAN_ID}/${TASK_ID}\"\n      exit 1\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n```\nPure doc-only / config-only / test-only tasks return `is_behavior_adding=false` and are exempt. When the gate trips, Read `$HOME/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-mvp-tdd.md` for the exact halt report format.\n</step>\n\n<step name=\"check_blocking_antipatterns\" priority=\"first\">\n**MANDATORY — Check for blocking anti-patterns before any other work.**\n\nLook for a `.continue-here.md` in the current phase directory:\n\n```bash\nls ${phase_dir}/.continue-here.md 2>/dev/null || true\n```\n\nIf `.continue-here.md` exists, parse its \"Critical Anti-Patterns\" table for rows with `severity` = `blocking`.\n\n**If one or more `blocking` anti-patterns are found:**\n\nThis step cannot be skipped. Before proceeding to `check_interactive_mode` or any other step, the agent must demonstrate understanding of each blocking anti-pattern by answering all three questions for each one:\n\n1. **What is this anti-pattern?** — Describe it in your own words, not by quoting the handoff.\n2. **How did it manifest?** — Explain the specific failure that caused it to be recorded.\n3. **What structural mechanism (not acknowledgment) prevents it?** — Name the concrete step, checklist item, or enforcement mechanism that stops recurrence.\n\nWrite these answers inline before continuing. If a blocking anti-pattern cannot be answered from the context in `.continue-here.md`, stop and ask the user for clarification.\n\n**If no `.continue-here.md` exists, or no `blocking` rows are found:** Proceed directly to `check_interactive_mode`.\n</step>\n\n<step name=\"check_interactive_mode\">\n**Parse `--interactive` flag from $ARGUMENTS.** If present, switch to interactive execution mode: plans run sequentially **inline** (no subagent spawning, ignoring wave grouping), reading `execute-plan.md` directly rather than dispatching `gsd-executor`. **Once per plan** (not per task), present a 4-option menu (execute / review-first / skip / stop) before starting that plan's tasks. Once executing, tasks run one at a time with only a brief pause after each — the agent stops mid-plan only if the user actually types something, it does not re-show the menu. After all plans, proceed to verification as normal. Full flow (the exact presentation format, the review-first sub-branch): `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/detail/elaboration.md` § 1.\n\n**Skip to handle_branching step** (interactive plans execute inline after grouping).\n</step>\n\n<step name=\"handle_branching\">\nCheck `branching_strategy` from init:\n\n**\"none\":** Read and execute `execute-phase/steps/protected-branch.md`.\n\n**\"phase\" or \"milestone\":** Use pre-computed `branch_name` from init.\n\nFork the new phase branch off `origin/HEAD` (the project's default branch), not the current HEAD — otherwise consecutive phases compound and stay unpushed (#2916). If `$BRANCH_NAME` already exists locally, reuse it as-is.\n\n```bash\nDEFAULT_BRANCH=$(gsd_run query git.base-branch 2>/dev/null \\\n  || git symbolic-ref --quiet --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null | sed 's|^origin/||' \\\n  || echo main)\n\nif git show-ref --verify --quiet \"refs/heads/$BRANCH_NAME\"; then\n  git switch \"$BRANCH_NAME\" || { echo \"ERROR: Could not switch to existing branch '$BRANCH_NAME'.\" >&2; exit 1; }\nelse\n  if ! git fetch --quiet origin \"$DEFAULT_BRANCH\"; then  # #2916\n    git show-ref --verify --quiet \"refs/remotes/origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" \\\n      || { echo \"ERROR: fetch origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH failed and no local copy exists. Refusing to create '$BRANCH_NAME' off current HEAD (#2916).\" >&2; exit 1; }\n    echo \"WARNING: fetch origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH failed; using local copy as base.\" >&2\n  fi\n  if [ -n \"$(git status --porcelain)\" ]; then\n    echo \"WARNING: Uncommitted changes will be carried onto '$BRANCH_NAME' (branched off origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH, not previous HEAD).\"\n  else\n    git switch --quiet \"$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null && git merge --ff-only --quiet \"origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || true\n  fi\n  # Pinned base (#2916); --no-track (#2498). #2639: warn if local ahead of origin.\n  AHEAD=$(git rev-list --count \"origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH..$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n  [ \"$AHEAD\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$AHEAD\" ] && echo \"WARNING: $DEFAULT_BRANCH is $AHEAD ahead of origin — '$BRANCH_NAME' won't include those commits (#2639).\" >&2\n  git checkout -b \"$BRANCH_NAME\" \"origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH\" --no-track \\\n    || { echo \"ERROR: Could not create '$BRANCH_NAME' from origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH (#2916).\" >&2; exit 1; }\nfi\n```\n\nAll subsequent commits go to this branch. User handles merging.\n</step>\n\n<step name=\"validate_phase\">\nFrom init JSON: `phase_dir`, `plan_count`, `incomplete_count`.\n\nReport: \"Found {plan_count} plans in {phase_dir} ({incomplete_count} incomplete)\"\n\n**Update STATE.md for phase start:**\n```bash\ngsd_run query state.begin-phase --phase \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" --name \"${PHASE_NAME}\" --plans \"${PLAN_COUNT}\"\n```\nThis updates Status, Last Activity, Current focus, Current Position, and plan counts in STATE.md so frontmatter and body text reflect the active phase immediately.\n</step>\n\n<step name=\"discover_and_group_plans\">\nLoad plan inventory with wave grouping in one call:\n\n```bash\nPLAN_INDEX=$(gsd_run query phase-plan-index \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")\n```\n\nParse JSON for: `phase`, `plans[]`, `waves`, `incomplete`, `runnable`, `ready_plans`, `has_checkpoints` — full per-plan fields and the #4628 readiness rules: read and follow `execute-phase/steps/ready-wave-gate.md`.\n\n**Filtering:** Skip plans where `has_summary: true`. Additionally skip any plan whose `blocked_by` array is non-empty (#2830) — it depends, directly or transitively, on a plan that halted at a designed stop rather than completing — and report it by name: \"Skipping {plan.id}: blocked by halted {blocked_by.join(', ')}\". Never silently drop a blocked plan from the report; it must appear by name with its reason, not merely vanish from the executable list. This rule is additive to the `has_summary` skip, not a replacement for it. Additionally skip any incomplete plan with `ready: false` (#4628 — see `execute-phase/steps/ready-wave-gate.md`; never dispatch a not-ready plan). If `--gaps-only`: also skip plans whose `gap_closure` is not `true` — but first confirm every plan object carries a `gap_closure` key. If any lacks it, the index cannot answer the filter (an older gsd-tools): STOP and report \"--gaps-only cannot read gap_closure from phase-plan-index — refusing to report an empty selection\" rather than filtering. A key the index never emitted must not surface as \"No matching incomplete plans\" (#4924). If `WAVE_FILTER` is set: also skip plans whose `wave` does not equal `WAVE_FILTER`.\n\n**Wave safety check:** If `WAVE_FILTER` is set and there are still incomplete plans in any lower wave that match the current execution mode, STOP and tell the user to finish earlier waves first. Do not let Wave 2+ execute while prerequisite earlier-wave plans remain incomplete.\n\n**If all filtered — do NOT exit unconditionally (#2868).** \"No plan work left\" and \"phase fully\ndone\" are different conditions: a run can be interrupted between the final wave's SUMMARY and\n`verify_phase_goal` (most commonly by a checkpoint plan that is retired but still writes a SUMMARY),\nleaving a phase that looks complete from every index yet never produced `*-VERIFICATION.md`. A\nthird condition looks identical to the first two by plan_count alone but is neither: some filtered\nplans were filtered because they are **blocked** (non-empty `blocked_by`, #2830), not because they\nare done. Blocked-and-incomplete must never be reported as finished.\n\n```bash\n# #5118: the owner's answer — `status` and the bare command it routes to. A non-zero exit\n# (an out-of-set report status) is a hard error: surface it, never read it as \"no status\".\nVERIFY_STATUS=$(gsd_run query verification status \"${PHASE_DIR}\" --pick status) || { echo \"verification status failed — see the error above\" >&2; exit 1; }\nVERIFY_ROUTE=$(gsd_run query verification status \"${PHASE_DIR}\" --pick route) || { echo \"verification status failed — see the error above\" >&2; exit 1; }\n# #3684: checkbox = marked-complete; report fields can claim a no-op write (#3685).\nANALYZE=$(gsd_run query roadmap.analyze)\nif [[ \"$ANALYZE\" == @file:* ]]; then ANALYZE=$(cat \"${ANALYZE#@file:}\"); fi\nPHASE_MARKED=$(echo \"$ANALYZE\"|jq -r --arg p \"$PHASE_NUMBER\" 'def n:sub(\"^0+(?=[0-9])\";\"\");.phases[]|select(((.number//.phase_number|tostring|n))==($p|n))|.roadmap_complete'|head -1)\n```\n\nEvaluate in this exact order — the first matching condition decides the outcome; do not evaluate\nlater conditions once one matches:\n\n1. **A filter is active** (`--gaps-only`, or `WAVE_FILTER` set): report \"No matching incomplete\n   plans\" → exit, unchanged. A filtered run finding nothing left in ITS slice says nothing about\n   whether the phase as a whole is done, and must never jump to verification.\n2. **No filter is active, and at least one filtered plan was skipped because of a non-empty\n   `blocked_by`** (irrespective of `VERIFY_STATUS`): the phase is NOT finished — it is **stuck on a\n   halt**. A plan with no SUMMARY and no dispatched work must never be treated as done merely\n   because nothing was left to filter. Report:\n   `\"Phase stuck: {blocked plan ids} blocked by halted {their blocked_by ids} — resolve the halt, do not resume verification.\"`\n   → exit. Do not fall through to condition 3; this is not a completion state.\n2b. **No filter is active, no blocked-plan skip occurred, and at least one filtered plan was skipped because `ready: false` (#4628)** — the phase is WAITING on incomplete predecessors, not finished: report it by name and exit before any completion state (`execute-phase/steps/ready-wave-gate.md`).\n3. **No filter is active, and every filtered plan was filtered by `has_summary` alone** (no\n   blocked-plan skip occurred) — branch on the owner's answer, never on a status word (#5118):\n   - **`VERIFY_ROUTE == execute-phase`** — the owner routes here when the verify step never ran\n     (`VERIFY_STATUS == missing`, #2868) and when covered source changed after the verifier ran\n     (#4682); on both sides of `PHASE_MARKED`. Report `$VERIFY_STATUS` with:\n     `\"All {plan_count} plans are summarized but no VERIFICATION.md exists — resuming at the phase gates (#2868).\"`\n     (or, for a stale report, \"…verification is stale — resuming at the phase gates to re-run the verifier (#4682).\")\n     SKIP `cross_ai_delegation`, `execute_waves` and `checkpoint_handling` — there is no wave work\n     to do — and continue directly at `aggregate_results`, NOT `code_review_gate`. `aggregate_results`\n     reads exclusively from on-disk `${PHASE_DIR}` artifacts (`*-SUMMARY.md`) and independent","numLines":400,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1410}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CFjx5ftcv8FZPinGcWJgPC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
