{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EV3wjQ9Esqj8JTu2WKqM98","type":"tool_result","content":"900\t     [ -z \"$WT_BRANCH\" ] || [ \"$WT_BRANCH\" = \"HEAD\" ] && continue\n901\t     echo \"Cleaning up residual worktree: $WT (branch: $WT_BRANCH)\"\n902\t     git worktree unlock \"$WT\" 2>/dev/null || true\n903\t     if ! git worktree remove \"$WT\" --force; then\n904\t       WT_NAME=$(basename \"$WT\")\n905\t       if [ -f \".git/worktrees/${WT_NAME}/locked\" ]; then\n906\t         echo \"⚠ Worktree $WT is locked — unlock failed; manual cleanup required:\"\n907\t         echo \"    git worktree unlock \\\"$WT\\\" && git worktree remove \\\"$WT\\\" --force && git branch -D \\\"$WT_BRANCH\\\"\"\n908\t       else\n909\t         echo \"⚠ Residual worktree at $WT — remove failed; manual cleanup required\"\n910\t       fi\n911\t     else\n912\t       git branch -D \"$WT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || true\n913\t     fi\n914\t   done < \"$WT_PATHS_FILE\"\n915\t   git worktree prune\n916\t   ```\n917\t\n918\t   **When to skip step 5.5:**\n919\t\n920\t   **If no plan in this wave used worktree isolation** (project-level `USE_WORKTREES=false` OR every plan in the wave had `USE_WORKTREES_FOR_PLAN=false` — i.e. `WAVE_WORKTREE_PLANS` from step 2.5 is empty): all agents ran on the main working tree — skip this step entirely.\n921\t\n922\t   **If the orchestrator merged via custom messages (cross-wave-dependency deviation):** the templated cleanup loop above was not triggered for those merges. Run the cleanup-tail snippet above instead. After the snippet completes, proceed to step 5.6.\n923\t\n924\t   **If at least one plan used worktrees but others did not:** still run this cleanup — it iterates over actual `git worktree list` output and only merges back the worktrees that were created, leaving sequential plans' commits on the main tree untouched.\n925\t\n926\t   **If no worktrees found at runtime:** Skip silently — agents may have been spawned without worktree isolation, or the orchestrator already cleaned them up.\n927\t\n928\t   If the user declines to merge a worktree or a worktree over-reached scope, apply the worktree recovery policy (`execute-phase/steps/worktree-recovery-policy.md`) — never default to editing `main`.\n929\t\n930\t5.6. **Post-merge build & test gate:**\n931\t\n932\t   After merging all worktrees in a wave (parallel mode), or after the last plan completes\n933\t   (serial mode), run a build and then the project's test suite to catch cross-plan\n934\t   integration issues that individual worktree self-checks cannot detect (e.g., conflicting\n935\t   type definitions, removed exports, import changes, link errors).\n936\t\n937\t   This addresses the Generator self-evaluation blind spot identified in Anthropic's\n938\t   harness engineering research: agents reliably report Self-Check: PASSED even when\n939\t   merging their work creates failures.\n940\t\n941\t   Read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/post-merge-gate.md`.\n942\t\n943\t5.7. **Post-wave shared artifact update (when at least one plan used worktrees, skip if tests failed):**\n944\t\n945\t   When **any** executor agent in this wave ran with `isolation=\"worktree\"`, that agent skipped STATE.md and ROADMAP.md updates to avoid last-merge-wins overwrites. The orchestrator is the single writer for these files. After worktrees are merged back, update shared artifacts once for every completed plan in the wave (worktree-mode plans **and** sequential plans that ran on the main tree but deferred to the orchestrator for tracking writes).\n946\t\n947\t   **Only update tracking when tests passed (TEST_EXIT=0).**\n948\t   If tests failed or timed out, skip the tracking update — plans should\n949\t   not be marked as complete when integration tests are failing or inconclusive.\n950\t\n951\t   ```bash\n952\t   # Guard: only update tracking if post-merge tests passed\n953\t   # Timeout (124) is treated as inconclusive — do NOT mark plans complete\n954\t   if [ \"${TEST_EXIT}\" -eq 0 ]; then\n955\t     # Update ROADMAP plan progress for each completed plan in this wave\n956\t     for plan_id in {completed_plan_ids}; do\n957\t       gsd_run query roadmap.update-plan-progress \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" \"${plan_id}\" \"complete\"\n958\t     done\n959\t\n960\t     # Only commit tracking files if they actually changed\n961\t     if ! git diff --quiet .planning/ROADMAP.md .planning/STATE.md 2>/dev/null; then\n962\t       gsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-${PHASE_NUMBER}): update tracking after wave ${N}\" --files .planning/ROADMAP.md .planning/STATE.md\n963\t     fi\n964\t   elif [ \"${TEST_EXIT}\" -eq 124 ]; then\n965\t     echo \"⚠ Skipping tracking update — test suite timed out. Plans remain in-progress. Run tests manually to confirm.\"\n966\t   else\n967\t     echo \"⚠ Skipping tracking update — post-merge tests failed (exit ${TEST_EXIT}). Plans remain in-progress until tests pass.\"\n968\t   fi\n969\t   ```\n970\t\n971\t   Where `WAVE_PLAN_IDS` is the space-separated list of plan IDs that completed in this wave.\n972\t\n973\t   **If no plan in this wave used worktrees** (project-level `USE_WORKTREES=false` OR `WAVE_WORKTREE_PLANS` is empty): sequential agents already updated STATE.md and ROADMAP.md themselves — skip this step.\n974\t\n975\t5.75. **Execute:wave:post capability dispatch:**\n976\t\n977\t   After worktree merge, post-merge tests, and tracking updates, dispatch capability hooks registered at `execute:wave:post`. The primary hook is the `ui.safety-gate` gate from the UI capability — it verifies that any frontend files changed in this wave conform to the UI-SPEC contract.\n978\t\n979\t   ```bash\n980\t   WAVE_POST_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:wave:post --raw)\n981\t   ```\n982\t\n983\t   Read the `activeHooks` array from `WAVE_POST_HOOKS_JSON` in-context (do NOT pipe through a shell parser).\n984\t\n985\t   **If `activeHooks` is empty or absent:** Skip silently to step 5.8.\n986\t\n987\t   **Contribution dispatch:** inject every `kind == \"contribution\"` fragment per @gsd-core/references/loop-hook-dispatch.md (skip when none), before the gates below.\n988\t\n989\t   **Step dispatch:** dispatch every `kind == \"step\"` hook per @gsd-core/references/loop-hook-dispatch.md (skip when none) — not one shape of one. A step here is advisory: it never blocks wave completion. ⚠ **Validate `ref.command` in-context before any shell use** (third-party manifest input) — loop-hook-dispatch.md § `step`. **`ref.skill == \"code-review\"` (#3661):** the generic contract's bare skill dispatch carries no phase argument, but `code-review.md`'s `initialize` step requires one (`PHASE_ARG=\"${1}\"`) or it reports \"Phase not found\" and exits — pass it explicitly, mirroring step `code_review_gate` in `execute-phase/steps/verify-phase-goal.md`: `Skill(skill=\"gsd-code-review\", args=\"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")`.\n990\t\n991\t   **For each active entry where `kind == \"gate\"`** (process in array order): read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/wave-post-gate-hooks.md` for the full evaluation contract (check validation, `onError`, blocking semantics, mapper spawn). A gate declared `blocking: false` — the `drift` capability's codebase-drift gate is one — is non-blocking by contract: it reports and the wave continues. When all active gates are processed without a blocking halt, continue to step 5.8.\n992\t\n993\t5.8. **Handle test gate failures (when `WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT > 0`):**\n994\t\n995\t   Read the count the post-merge gate recorded (#4915); a shell variable set in step 5.6 is gone by now:\n996\t\n997\t   ```bash\n998\t   # gsd-handoff:begin wave-failure-read\n999\t   _GSD_HANDOFF=\"$( { git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir 2>/dev/null || echo \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gsd-$(pwd | cksum | cut -d' ' -f1)\"; } )/gsd-handoff\"; mkdir -p \"$_GSD_HANDOFF\"\n1000\t   WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT=$(wc -l < \"$_GSD_HANDOFF/wave-failures\" 2>/dev/null | tr -d ' ' || true); WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT=${WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT:-0}\n1001\t   echo \"WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT=${WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT}\"\n1002\t   # gsd-handoff:end wave-failure-read\n1003\t   ```\n1004\t\n1005\t   ```\n1006\t   ## ⚠ Post-Merge Test Failure (cumulative failures: ${WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT})\n1007\t\n1008\t   Wave {N} worktrees merged successfully, but {M} tests fail after merge.\n1009\t   This typically indicates conflicting changes across parallel plans\n1010\t   (e.g., type definitions, shared imports, API contracts).\n1011\t\n1012\t   Failed tests:\n1013\t   {first 10 lines of failure output}\n1014\t\n1015\t   Options:\n1016\t   1. Fix now (recommended) — resolve conflicts before next wave\n1017\t   2. Continue — failures may compound in subsequent waves\n1018\t   ```\n1019\t\n1020\t   Note: If `WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT > 1`, strongly recommend \"Fix now\" — compounding\n1021\t   failures across multiple waves become exponentially harder to diagnose.\n1022\t\n1023\t   If \"Fix now\": diagnose failures (import conflicts, missing types,\n1024\t   or changed function signatures from parallel plans modifying the same module).\n1025\t   Fix, commit as `fix: resolve post-merge conflicts from wave {N}`, re-run tests.\n1026\t\n1027\t   **Why this matters:** Worktree isolation means each agent's Self-Check passes\n1028\t   in isolation. But when merged, add/add conflicts in shared files (models, registries,\n1029\t   CLI entry points) can silently drop code. The post-merge gate catches this before\n1030\t   the next wave builds on a broken foundation.\n1031\t\n1032\t6. **Report completion — spot-check claims first:**\n1033\t\n1034\t   **Wave-close heartbeat (#2410):** after spot-checks finish (pass or fail),\n1035\t   before the `## Wave {N} Complete` summary, emit as a literal line:\n1036\t\n1037\t   ```\n1038\t   [checkpoint] phase {PHASE_NUMBER} wave {N}/{M} complete, {P}/{Q} plans done ({wave_success}/{wave_plan_count} ok)\n1039\t   ```\n1040\t\n1041\t   For each SUMMARY.md:\n1042\t   - Verify first 2 files from `key-files.created` exist on disk\n1043\t   - Check `gsd_run check evaluation-scope --plan \"{phase}-{plan}\" --commits-only --raw` returns `commits` with ≥1 entry (commits on THIS branch only — #5164; a commit that lives only on another branch does not satisfy the check; exit `69` means the scope could not be resolved, which fails the spot-check, never \"no commits yet\")\n1044\t   - Check for `## Self-Check: FAILED` marker\n1045\t\n1046\t   If ANY spot-check fails: report which plan failed, route to failure handler — ask \"Retry plan?\" or \"Continue with remaining waves?\"\n1047\t\n1048\t   If pass:\n1049\t   ```\n1050\t   ---\n1051\t   ## Wave {N} Complete\n1052\t\n1053\t   **{Plan ID}: {Plan Name}**\n1054\t   {What was built — from SUMMARY.md}\n1055\t   {Notable deviations, if any}\n1056\t\n1057\t   {If more waves: what this enables for next wave}\n1058\t   ---\n1059\t   ```\n1060\t\n1061\t7. **Handle failures:**\n1062\t   **Step 7.0 — classify before branching (#3095):**\n1063\t   ```bash\n1064\t   CLASS_JSON=$(gsd_run query agent.classify-failure -- \"$AGENT_RETURN_BODY\")\n1065\t   CLASS=$(echo \"$CLASS_JSON\" | jq -r '.class')\n1066\t   SENTINEL=$(echo \"$CLASS_JSON\" | jq -r '.sentinel // empty')\n1067\t   RETRY_AFTER=$(echo \"$CLASS_JSON\" | jq -r '.retryAfterSeconds // empty')\n1068\t   if [ -n \"$RETRY_AFTER\" ]; then RETRY_HINT=\"  Provider hinted retry-after: ${RETRY_AFTER}s\"; else RETRY_HINT=\"\"; fi\n1069\t   ```\n1070\t   One classifier branch handles sentinels across Claude/Copilot/Codex/Antigravity. Reference: `docs/research/provider-rate-limit-signals.md`.\n1071\t   **Abnormal ends reconcile first (#4217):** an abnormal session end (`turn_aborted`-class) routes through the step-4 artifact reconciliation BEFORE classifying the failure — artifacts decide.\n1072\t   **Step 7.1 — `class == \"quota-exceeded\"`:** follow the quota-recovery fragment below.\n1073\t   **Step 7.2 — `class == \"classify-handoff-bug\"`:**\n1074\t   If error contains `classifyHandoffIfNeeded is not defined`, treat as Claude runtime bug. Run the same step-5 spot-checks; PASS => treat as success, FAIL => fall through.\n1075\t   **Step 7.3 — `class == \"unknown-failure\"`:**\n1076\t   Report failed plan and ask Continue/Stop; continuing may cascade into dependent plan failures.\n1077\t\n1078\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-quota-recovery.md\n1079\t\n1080\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-between-wave-reset.md\n1081\t\n1082\t8. **Execute checkpoint plans between waves** — see `<checkpoint_handling>`.\n1083\t9. **Proceed to next wave.**\n1084\t</step>\n1085\t<step name=\"checkpoint_handling\">\n1086\tPlans with `autonomous: false` require user interaction.\n1087\t**Auto-mode checkpoint handling:**\n1088\tRead auto-advance config (chain flag OR user preference — same boolean as `check.auto-mode`):\n1089\t```bash\n1090\tAUTO_MODE=$(gsd_run query check auto-mode --pick active 2>/dev/null)\n1091\t```\n1092\t\n1093\tWhen executor returns a checkpoint AND `AUTO_MODE` is `true`:\n1094\t- **human-verify** → Auto-spawn continuation agent with `{user_response}` = `\"approved\"`. Log `⚡ Auto-approved checkpoint`. **Except `blocking-human`.**\n1095\t- **decision** → `auto_select` present: auto-spawn with `{user_response}` = that option, log `⚡ Auto-selected: [option]`. Absent: present to user (#4095). **Except `blocking-human`.**\n1096\t- **human-action** → Present to user (existing behavior below). Auth gates cannot be automated.\n1097\t\n1098\t<!-- gsd:protected -->\n1099\t**Carve-out — overrides all branches above.** If the returned `Gate:` is `blocking-human` (precondition-unmet, #3210), or its `<what-built>` mentions `Package verification required before install` or `Package install failed — human verification required`, never auto-approve or auto-select. Present to user (standard flow). Log `⛔ blocking-human gate — auto-mode suspended`.\n1100\t\n1101\t**Standard flow (not auto-mode, human-action, or blocking-human):**\n1102\t\n1103\t1. Spawn agent for checkpoint plan\n1104\t2. Agent runs until checkpoint task or auth gate → returns structured state\n1105\t3. Agent return includes: completed tasks table, current task + blocker, checkpoint type/details, what's awaited\n1106\t4. **Present to user:**\n1107\t   ```\n1108\t   ## Checkpoint: [Type]\n1109\t\n1110\t   **Plan:** 03-03 Dashboard Layout\n1111\t   **Progress:** 2/3 tasks complete\n1112\t\n1113\t   [Checkpoint Details from agent return]\n1114\t   [Awaiting section from agent return]\n1115\t   ```\n1116\t5. User responds: \"approved\"/\"done\" | issue description | decision selection\n1117\t6. **Spawn continuation agent (NOT resume)** using continuation-prompt.md template:\n1118\t   - `{completed_tasks_table}`: From checkpoint return\n1119\t   - `{resume_task_number}` + `{resume_task_name}`: Current task\n1120\t   - `{user_response}`: What user provided\n1121\t   - `{resume_instructions}`: Based on checkpoint type\n1122\t7. Continuation agent verifies previous commits, continues from resume point\n1123\t8. Repeat until plan completes or user stops\n1124\t\n1125\t**Why fresh agent, not resume:** Resume relies on internal serialization that breaks with parallel tool calls. Fresh agents with explicit state are more reliable.\n1126\t\n1127\t**Checkpoints in parallel waves:** Agent pauses and returns while other parallel agents may complete. Present checkpoint, spawn continuation, wait for all before next wave.\n1128\t</step>\n1129\t\n1130\t<step name=\"aggregate_results\">\n1131\tAfter all waves:\n1132\t\n1133\t```markdown\n1134\t## Phase {X}: {Name} Execution Complete\n1135\t\n1136\t**Waves:** {N} | **Plans:** {M}/{total} complete\n1137\t\n1138\t| Wave | Plans | Status |\n1139\t|------|-------|--------|\n1140\t| 1 | plan-01, plan-02 | ✓ Complete |\n1141\t| CP | plan-03 | ✓ Verified |\n1142\t| 2 | plan-04 | ✓ Complete |\n1143\t\n1144\t### Plan Details\n1145\t1. **03-01**: [one-liner from SUMMARY.md]\n1146\t2. **03-02**: [one-liner from SUMMARY.md]\n1147\t\n1148\t### Issues Encountered\n1149\t[Aggregate from SUMMARYs, or \"None\"]\n1150\t```\n1151\t\n1152\tThe `verify:post` hook dispatch and the SECURITY threats-open gate are the first step of the shared\n1153\tverification step (`verify_post_security_gate` in `verify_phase_goal` below), so verify-work's\n1154\tre-verification route runs them too (#5118).\n1155\t</step>\n1156\t\n1157\tIf `section_manifest` is `null` or `\"partial-wave\"` is in its `included` list: read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/partial-wave.md`. Otherwise skip — do not read the file.\n1158\t\n1159\t<step name=\"verify_phase_goal\">\n1160\tVerify phase achieved its GOAL, not just completed tasks: read and execute\n1161\t`gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/verify-phase-goal.md` — the ONE verification action, the\n1162\twhole sequence (the `verify:post` dispatch with the SECURITY threats-open gate, `code_review_gate`\n1163\twith its TDD escalation, the gap-closure parent-artifact close, the manifest-gated `regression_gate`,\n1164\tthe verifier dispatch, the fingerprint, and the owner's `verification.status` read with stderr\n1165\tkept), shared with verify-work (#5118). If it stopped (TDD block, regression abort, refused\n1166\treport), stop here.\n1167\t\n1168\t**TDD review escalation (#4011):** the `tdd.review-checkpoint` gate is advisory (`blocking: false`)\n1169\texcept when `TDD_MODE=true` AND `GATE_RESULT.block == true` — no MVP condition — where the shared\n1170\tstep escalates the end-of-phase review to blocking: refuse to mark the phase complete and present\n1171\t`Phase blocked: {N} TDD plan(s) violate the RED→GREEN gate sequence under TDD.` Never proceed to\n1172\t`close_parent_artifacts`, `verify_phase_goal`'s verifier or `phase.complete` past that block. Full\n1173\tcontract: `gsd-core/references/execute-mvp-tdd.md` and the step's `code_review_gate`.\n1174\t\n1175\tRoute on `$STATUS`: if `passed`, proceed to update_roadmap. Otherwise keep the phase pending — present `$NEXT_ACTION` to the user and, when `$NEXT_COMMAND` is non-empty, show it as the next command to run. The query covers every case — including no report (`missing`) and no phase directory (`phase_dir_not_found`) — and a status outside the closed set is a hard error the shared step already halted on, so no per-status arm needs to be listed here.\n1176\t\n1177\t**If human_needed:**\n1178\t\n1179\t**Step A: Persist human verification items as UAT file.**\n1180\t\n1181\tCreate `{phase_dir}/{phase_num}-UAT.md` using UAT template format:\n1182\t\n1183\t```markdown\n1184\t---\n1185\tstatus: testing\n1186\tphase: {phase_num}-{phase_name}\n1187\tsource: [{phase_num}-VERIFICATION.md]\n1188\tstarted: [now ISO]\n1189\tupdated: [now ISO]\n1190\t---\n1191\t\n1192\t## Current Test\n1193\t\n1194\tnumber: 1\n1195\tname: {first human_verification item description}\n1196\texpected: |\n1197\t  {expected behavior from VERIFICATION.md}\n1198\tawaiting: user response\n1199\t\n1200\t## Tests\n1201\t\n1202\t{For each human_verification item from VERIFICATION.md:}\n1203\t\n1204\t### {N}. {item description}\n1205\texpected: {expected behavior from VERIFICATION.md}\n1206\tresult: [pending]\n1207\t\n1208\t## Summary\n1209\t\n1210\ttotal: {count}\n1211\tpassed: 0\n1212\tissues: 0\n1213\tpending: {count}\n1214\tskipped: 0\n1215\tblocked: 0\n1216\t\n1217\t## Gaps\n1218\t```\n1219\t\n1220\tCommit the file:\n1221\t```bash\n1222\tgsd_run query commit \"test({phase_num}): persist human verification items as UAT\" --files \"{phase_dir}/{phase_num}-UAT.md\"\n1223\t```\n1224\t\n1225\t**Step B: Present to user**:\n1226\t\n1227\t```\n1228\t## ◷ Phase {X}: {Name} — Human Verification Needed\n1229\t\n1230\tAll automated checks passed. {N} item(s) require human testing before this phase can be marked complete:\n1231\t\n1232\t{From VERIFICATION.md human_verification section}\n1233\t\n1234\tTests saved to `{phase_num}-UAT.md`.\n1235\t\n1236\tWhen ready to run the tests:\n1237\t\n1238\t`/gsd-verify-work {X} ${GSD_WS}`\n1239\t\n1240\tVerify-work will walk you through each item and mark the phase complete when all tests pass.\n1241\t```\n1242\t\n1243\t**Do NOT advance the phase from this branch.** Phase completion is handled by verify-work's auto-transition after UAT passes.\n1244\t\n1245\t**If user acknowledges without reporting issues (including \"ok\", \"noted\", \"ack\", \"got it\", \"approved\", \"done\", \"yes\", \"pass\", or similar):** Stop. The phase remains pending. No further orchestrator action — wait for the user to run `/gsd-verify-work`.\n1246\t\n1247\t**If user reports issues now:** Proceed to gap closure.\n1248\t\n1249\t**If gaps_found:**\n1250\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-requirement-revert.md\n1251\t```\n1252\t## ⚠ Phase {X}: {Name} — Gaps Found\n1253\t\n1254\t**Score:** {N}/{M} must-haves verified\n1255\t**Report:** {phase_dir}/{phase_num}-VERIFICATION.md\n1256\t\n1257\t### What's Missing\n1258\t{Gap summaries from VERIFICATION.md}\n1259\t\n1260\t---\n1261\t## ▶ Next Up — [${PROJECT_CODE}] ${PROJECT_TITLE}\n1262\t\n1263\t`/clear` then:\n1264\t\n1265\t`/gsd-plan-phase {X} --gaps ${GSD_WS}`\n1266\t\n1267\tAlso: `cat {phase_dir}/{phase_num}-VERIFICATION.md` — full report\n1268\tAlso: `/gsd-verify-work {X} ${GSD_WS}` — manual testing first\n1269\t```\n1270\t\n1271\tGap closure cycle: `/gsd-plan-phase {X} --gaps ${GSD_WS}` reads VERIFICATION.md → creates gap plans with `gap_closure: true` → user runs `/gsd-execute-phase {X} --gaps-only ${GSD_WS}` → verifier re-runs.\n1272\t</step>\n1273\t\n1274\tThe `gap-closure-artifacts` section is evaluated inside the shared verification step\n1275\t(`verify_phase_goal` above) — between its code-review gate and its regression gate, where it ran\n1276\tbefore #5118 — gated on this id exactly as every section here is gated.\n1277\t\n1278\tThe `regression-gate` section is evaluated inside the shared verification step (`verify_phase_goal`\n1279\tabove), which gates it on this id exactly as every section here is gated (#5118).\n1280\t\n1281\t<step name=\"update_roadmap\">\n1282\t**Mark phase complete and update all tracking files:**\n1283\t\n1284\t```bash\n1285\tCOMPLETION=$(gsd_run query phase.complete \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")\n1286\t```\n1287\t\n1288\tThe CLI handles:\n1289\t- Marking phase checkbox `[x]` with completion date\n1290\t- Updating Progress table (Status → Complete, date)\n1291\t- Updating plan count to final\n1292\t- Advancing STATE.md to next phase\n1293\t- Updating REQUIREMENTS.md traceability\n1294\t- Scanning for verification debt (returns `warnings` array)\n1295\t\n1296\tExtract from result: `next_phase`, `next_phase_name`, `is_last_phase`, `warnings`, `has_warnings`.\n1297\t\n1298\t**If has_warnings is true**:\n1299\t```\n1300\t## Phase {X} marked complete with {N} warnings:\n1301\t\n1302\t{list each warning}\n1303\t\n1304\tThese items are tracked and will appear in `/gsd-progress` and `/gsd-audit-uat`.\n1305\t```\n1306\t\n1307\t```bash\n1308\tgsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-{X}): complete phase execution\" --files .planning/ROADMAP.md .planning/STATE.md .planning/REQUIREMENTS.md {phase_dir}/*-VERIFICATION.md\n1309\t```\n1310\t</step>\n1311\t\n1312\t<step name=\"auto_copy_learnings\">\n1313\t**Auto-extract and copy phase learnings to global store (when enabled).**\n1314\t\n1315\tThis step runs AFTER phase completion and SUMMARY.md is written. It produces the phase's\n1316\tlearnings artifact (the sole producer is otherwise the user-invoked\n1317\t`/gsd-extract-learnings`) and copies it to the global learnings store at\n1318\t`~/.gsd/knowledge/`.\n1319\t\n1320\t**Check config gate:**\n1321\t```bash\n1322\tGL_ENABLED=$(gsd_run query config-get features.global_learnings --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"false\")\n1323\t```\n1324\t\n1325\t**If `GL_ENABLED` is not `true`:** Skip this step entirely (feature disabled by default).\n1326\t\n1327\t**If enabled:**\n1328\t\n1329\t1. Run the `extract-learnings` workflow for the JUST-COMPLETED phase (its\n1330\t   `write_learnings` step writes `{phase_dir}/{PADDED_PHASE}-LEARNINGS.md`). Extraction\n1331\t   failure must NOT block phase completion — report the failure and continue.\n1332\t2. Copy the phase artifact to the global store:\n1333\t```bash\n1334\tgsd_run query learnings.copy 2>/dev/null || echo \"⚠ Learnings copy failed — continuing\"\n1335\t```\n1336\tCopy failure must NOT block phase completion.\n1337\t</step>\n1338\t\n1339\t<step name=\"close_phase_todos\">\n1340\t**Auto-close todos whose `resolves_phase` matches this phase (#2433)**, after `update_roadmap`.\n1341\t\n1342\t```bash\n1343\tshopt -s nullglob 2>/dev/null; setopt NULL_GLOB 2>/dev/null\n1344\tPENDING_DIR=\".planning/todos/pending\"\n1345\tCOMPLETED_DIR=\".planning/todos/completed\"\n1346\tmkdir -p \"$COMPLETED_DIR\"\n1347\tPHASE_NUM=\"${PHASE_NUMBER}\"\n1348\t#2576\n1349\tnormalize_phase_num() {\n1350\t  printf '%s' \"${1//\\\"/}\" | sed 's/^0*\\([0-9]\\)/\\1/'\n1351\t}\n1352\tPHASE_NUM_NORM=$(normalize_phase_num \"$PHASE_NUM\")\n1353\tCLOSED=()\n1354\tfor TODO_FILE in \"$PENDING_DIR\"/*.md; do\n1355\t  [ -f \"$TODO_FILE\" ] || continue\n1356\t  RP=$(awk '/^---/{c++;next} c==1 && /^resolves_phase:/{print $2;exit} c==2{exit}' \"$TODO_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n1357\t  RP_NORM=$(normalize_phase_num \"$RP\")\n1358\t  [ -n \"$RP_NORM\" ] && [ \"$RP_NORM\" = \"$PHASE_NUM_NORM\" ] || continue\n1359\t  mv \"$TODO_FILE\" \"$COMPLETED_DIR/\"\n1360\t  CLOSED+=(\"$(basename \"$TODO_FILE\")\")\n1361\tdone\n1362\tif [ ${#CLOSED[@]} -gt 0 ]; then\n1363\t  ADDED=(); REMOVED=()\n1364\t  for f in \"${CLOSED[@]}\"; do ADDED+=(\"$COMPLETED_DIR/$f\"); REMOVED+=(\"$PENDING_DIR/$f\"); done\n1365\t  gsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-${PHASE_NUMBER}): close ${#CLOSED[@]} resolved todo(s)\" --files \"${ADDED[@]}\" .planning/STATE.md --files-removed \"${REMOVED[@]}\" || true\n1366\t  echo \"◆ Closed ${#CLOSED[@]} todo(s) for Phase ${PHASE_NUMBER}:\"; printf '  ✓ %s\\n' \"${CLOSED[@]}\"\n1367