econd failover window and reports before the 4-minute page.</pros>\n47\t      <cons>Holds a worker slot for up to two minutes per stalled call.</cons>\n48\t    </option>\n49\t    <option id=\"budget-300\">\n50\t      <name>300 seconds</name>\n51\t      <pros>Survives even a slow failover with margin.</pros>\n52\t      <cons>Longer than the 4-minute pager threshold, so a dead upstream pages someone first.</cons>\n53\t    </option>\n54\t  </options>\n55\t  <resume-signal>Select: budget-30, budget-120, or budget-300</resume-signal>\n56\t</task>\n57\t\n58\t<task type=\"auto\">\n59\t  <name>Task 2: Implement probe/budget.py with the chosen budget</name>\n60\t  <files>probe/__init__.py, probe/budget.py</files>\n61\t  <action>\n62\tCreate an empty `probe/__init__.py`. Create `probe/budget.py` defining `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS: int` set to the\n63\tvalue chosen in Task 1, and `deadline_after(start_secs: float) -> float` returning\n64\t`start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS`. Do not edit `tests/test_budget.py`.\n65\t  </action>\n66\t  <verify>\n67\t    <automated>python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v</automated>\n68\t  </verify>\n69\t  <acceptance_criteria>\n70\t    - `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` exits 0 and reports `Ran 2 tests` and `OK`\n71\t    - `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` equals the option chosen in Task 1\n72\t  </acceptance_criteria>\n73\t  <done>The module holds the chosen budget and the existing test passes.</done>\n74\t</task>\n75\t\n76\t</tasks>\n77\t\n78\t<verification>\n79\t`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes.\n80\t</verification>\n81\t\n82\t<success_criteria>\n83\t- `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` is one of 30, 120 or 300 and `deadline_after` adds it to a start time.\n84\t</success_criteria>\n85\t\n86\t<output>\n87\tCreate `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-SUMMARY.md` when done.\n88\t</output>\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016hmGB6QEwtYjCjN7ULZ38G","agent_id":"a88a0ba3eec333e69","session_id":"uuid-4","uuid":"uuid-188"